course: dictionary
lesson: 11798
title: Bereaved: a gentle word about loss
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Bereaved describes a person who has lost someone close to them, usually a family member or friend, because that person has died. «After the storm, the bereaved family planted a tree in their garden.» The clue is the planting, which shows the family is sad about someone who has died.
explain: Bereaved can also be a noun, as in «the bereaved». It means the people who are grieving after a death. «The school sent cards of support to the bereaved.» Here the cards are for the people who have lost someone.
explain: Look at the words around bereaved. Words like family, recently, support and care tell you the word is about grief and comfort, not about being happy or angry. Ask yourself: who has lost someone, and how are others helping them?
explain: Bereaved is a careful, gentle word. It tells the reader that someone is grieving without saying more than is needed, which is why grown-ups use it in news, in churches and in letters of sympathy.
fact: Bereaved means having lost a close family member or friend because they died.
fact: «The bereaved» means the people who are grieving after someone has died.
fact: «Recently bereaved» means someone lost a loved one not long ago.
fact: «Support for the bereaved» means help and care given to people who are grieving.
fact: Schools and churches can offer care for bereaved children.
exercise: «Her grandad died last week, so she is now bereaved.» What does bereaved mean? | *Having lost someone close because they died | Being new to a school | Moving house to a new town | Feeling very hungry
exercise: «The school sent a card of support to the bereaved.» Who are the bereaved in this sentence? | The children who drew the pictures | *The people who are grieving | The teachers who wrote the card | The workers at the post office
exercise: Which phrase means a family that lost someone not long ago? | A family on holiday | *A recently bereaved family | A bereaved family | A happy family
test: «After the flood, the bereaved village held a quiet service.» What does bereaved suggest here? | People who are cold and wet | People who are leaving for a holiday | People who won a prize | *People grieving for loved ones who died
test: Priya says bereaved means angry. Why is she wrong? | Bereaved means lost in a busy shop | Bereaved means very angry at everyone | Bereaved means very tired after a race | *Bereaved means grieving for someone who has died
exam: What does «bereaved children» mean? | Children who are very fast runners | *Children who have lost someone close because they died | Children who have just moved to a new town | Children who love to draw
